{
  "version": 2,
  "note": "Holiday theme packs (card 2/9). Each pack is a pure CSS-variable override applied on :root while the guild has the pack opted in AND the current date falls in one of the pack's windows. No pack contains selectors, URLs, or script — only token names and literal values. Packs re-declare only the tokens that tint the season; every other token (surface-3, text-faint, spacing, radius, typography) inherits from the active base theme, so each pack layers cleanly over all 5 base themes. Window format: 'window' is a single {month: 1-12, startDay, endDay} (inclusive day-of-month bounds, no New Year span); 'windows' is an array of such objects — a pack is active when ANY window matches (used by easter to approximate the movable spring window). KNOWN LIMITATION: the month+day mechanism cannot track the movable date of Easter itself; the easter pack approximates Mar 25 - Apr 24 as two fixed windows and may be off by up to a week in a given year. Opt-in: packs are NOT auto-active for everyone — a guild must enable the pack via the theme picker (guild_theme_settings.holiday_theme). Backward compat: 'winter' remains an alias of 'xmas'.",
  "themes": {
    "none": {
      "label": "None",
      "vars": {}
    },
    "halloween": {
      "label": "Halloween",
      "window": { "month": 10, "startDay": 20, "endDay": 31 },
      "vars": {
        "--dzc-bg": "#150b06",
        "--dzc-bg-tint": "#1a0e07",
        "--dzc-surface": "#1d0f08",
        "--dzc-surface-2": "#271509",
        "--dzc-surface-3": "#331d0c",
        "--dzc-border": "#4a2e17",
